## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

1. **`parser`** · [ticket #1](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1):
   the shared parser reads every date month first, and day-first tenants get the day and month
   swapped. The `parser` row above, without the reports read as a one-day move. This is the bug
   the queued fix is for.
2. **`hint`** · [ticket #2](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2):
   the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants' people type
   month first, as told, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. The `hint` row above. It
   looks like the parser bug, but the parser fix does not touch it: the form's hint does.
3. **`one-day`** · [ticket #3](https://github.com/lbojalkowski-bf/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3):
   the date moves by one day, not by a month swap. One meeting shows Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday
   in Toronto, an invite arrives before the booking, "every booking in June is one day off". The
   reports read as a one-day move, under the table. The tenant rule files them under `parser`;
   the likely cause is a date converted between time zones, which neither fix touches.

## How the reports were split

1. One id, one report: rows the export repeats count once.
2. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) is its own problem.
3. Every other report takes its cause from its tenant and channel (`causes.ts`), not from the
   intake tag, which is a guess from the reporter's browser.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why one ticket hid three

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Reports about
different bugs use the same words ("Date is wrong"), so they landed in one ticket. Its own
consequence says engineering merges separate tickets later; nobody splits merged ones. A later
decision record should replace it: merge on cause (tenant, form, channel), not on subject.

